    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Vacation of office by Presiding Officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person holding office as Presiding Officer vacates the office:\n(a) immediately before a Presiding Officer is elected at the first\nmeeting of the Assembly after a general election;\n(b) when the person resigns office as Presiding Officer;\n(c) when the person ceases to be a member of the Assembly (not\nbecause of a general election); or\n(d) when an absolute majority of the members of the Assembly\nvote in favour of the person’s removal from office.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person holding office as Presiding Officer vacates the office:\n(a) immediately before a Presiding Officer is elected at the first\nmeeting of the Assembly after a general election;\n(b) when the person resigns office as Presiding Officer;\n(c) when the person ceases to be a member of the Assembly (not\nbecause of a general election); or\n(d) when an absolute majority of the members of the Assembly\nvote in favour of the person’s removal from office.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-12-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8603351d9a6b9e0a58c859e9153a6ee6bd547b7c97add622791fb9f959a0d833",
      "skos:note": "A person holding office as Presiding Officer must vacate the office under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Vacation of office by Presiding Officer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person holding office as Presiding Officer vacates the office:\n(a) immediately before a Presiding Officer is elected at the first\nmeeting of the Assembly after a general election;\n(b) when the person resigns office as Presiding Officer;\n(c) when the person ceases to be a member of the Assembly (not\nbecause of a general election); or\n(d) when an absolute majority of the members of the Assembly\nvote in favour of the person’s removal from office."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-12-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
