    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Times of meetings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), the Assembly shall meet:\n(a) within 7 days after the result of a general election is declared;\nand\n(b) within 7 days after a written request for a meeting, signed by\nsuch number of members as is fixed by enactment, is\ndelivered to the Presiding Officer.\n(2) The Presiding Officer shall, by notice published in the Territory\nGazette, convene a meeting when it is necessary to do so to comply\nwith subsection (1).\n(3) If the Presiding Officer is required by subsection (2) to convene a\nmeeting within a particular period and:\n(a) the office of Presiding Officer is vacant, whether or not a\nperson has been previously elected to the office; or\n(b) the Presiding Officer is unable, or refuses or fails, to convene\na meeting within that period;\nthe Commonwealth Minister shall, by notice published in the\nCommonwealth Gazette, convene the meeting within that period or,\nif that is not practicable, within 7 days after that period.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), the Assembly shall meet:\n(a) within 7 days after the result of a general election is declared;\nand\n(b) within 7 days after a written request for a meeting, signed by\nsuch number of members as is fixed by enactment, is\ndelivered to the Presiding Officer.\n(2) The Presiding Officer shall, by notice published in the Territory\nGazette, convene a meeting when it is necessary to do so to comply\nwith subsection (1).\n(3) If the Presiding Officer is required by subsection (2) to convene a\nmeeting within a particular period and:\n(a) the office of Presiding Officer is vacant, whether or not a\nperson has been previously elected to the office; or\n(b) the Presiding Officer is unable, or refuses or fails, to convene\na meeting within that period;\nthe Commonwealth Minister shall, by notice published in the\nCommonwealth Gazette, convene the meeting within that period or,\nif that is not practicable, within 7 days after that period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-17-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-17-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5347824b3e38e60e85a38da40c1271e284dcff28a5f9e70e771414ceab2046b3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Times of meetings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), the Assembly shall meet:\n(a) within 7 days after the result of a general election is declared;\nand\n(b) within 7 days after a written request for a meeting, signed by\nsuch number of members as is fixed by enactment, is\ndelivered to the Presiding Officer.\n(2) The Presiding Officer shall, by notice published in the Territory\nGazette, convene a meeting when it is necessary to do so to comply\nwith subsection (1).\n(3) If the Presiding Officer is required by subsection (2) to convene a\nmeeting within a particular period and:\n(a) the office of Presiding Officer is vacant, whether or not a\nperson has been previously elected to the office; or\n(b) the Presiding Officer is unable, or refuses or fails, to convene\na meeting within that period;\nthe Commonwealth Minister shall, by notice published in the\nCommonwealth Gazette, convene the meeting within that period or,\nif that is not practicable, within 7 days after that period."
    },
