    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Procedure at meetings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1) At a meeting of the Assembly, a quorum is formed by an absolute\nmajority of the members.\n(2) Questions arising at a meeting shall be decided by a majority of the\nvotes of the members present and voting, unless a special majority\nis required by the standing rules and orders.\n(3) The member presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote only,\nand, if the votes on a question are equal, the question shall pass in\nthe negative.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) At a meeting of the Assembly, a quorum is formed by an absolute\nmajority of the members.\n(2) Questions arising at a meeting shall be decided by a majority of the\nvotes of the members present and voting, unless a special majority\nis required by the standing rules and orders.\n(3) The member presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote only,\nand, if the votes on a question are equal, the question shall pass in\nthe negative.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-18-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-18-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-18-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bee06e61eb4bf0c78cca47b4a5ac4f7078a363569c1f57ccbf9c5aa712872d3d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Procedure at meetings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At a meeting of the Assembly, a quorum is formed by an absolute\nmajority of the members.\n(2) Questions arising at a meeting shall be decided by a majority of the\nvotes of the members present and voting, unless a special majority\nis required by the standing rules and orders.\n(3) The member presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote only,\nand, if the votes on a question are equal, the question shall pass in\nthe negative."
    },
