    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Powers, privileges and immunities of Assembly",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\npowers includes privileges and immunities, but does not include\nlegislative powers.\n(2) Without limiting the generality of section 22, the Assembly may\nalso make laws:\n(a) declaring the powers of the Assembly and of its members and\ncommittees, but so that the powers so declared do not exceed\n\n\nPowers of Legislative Assembly  Part IV\n\nSection 25\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nthe powers for the time being of the House of\nRepresentatives or of its members or committees; and\n(b) providing for the manner in which powers so declared may\nbe exercised or upheld.\n(3) Until the Assembly makes a law with respect to its powers, the\nAssembly and its members and committees have the same powers\nas the powers for the time being of the House of Representatives\nand its members and committees.\n(4) Nothing in this section empowers the Assembly to imprison or fine\na person.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this section:\npowers includes privileges and immunities, but does not include\nlegislative powers.\n(2) Without limiting the generality of section 22, the Assembly may\nalso make laws:\n(a) declaring the powers of the Assembly and of its members and\ncommittees, but so that the powers so declared do not exceed\n\n\nPowers of Legislative Assembly  Part IV\n\nSection 25\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nthe powers for the time being of the House of\nRepresentatives or of its members or committees; and\n(b) providing for the manner in which powers so declared may\nbe exercised or upheld.\n(3) Until the Assembly makes a law with respect to its powers, the\nAssembly and its members and committees have the same powers\nas the powers for the time being of the House of Representatives\nand its members and committees.\n(4) Nothing in this section empowers the Assembly to imprison or fine\na person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-24-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-24-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-24-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-24-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c36e2d2ef261d7dccfb8eb46967d5e62ad403667993544092988dbe0472a1d48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Powers, privileges and immunities of Assembly",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\npowers includes privileges and immunities, but does not include\nlegislative powers.\n(2) Without limiting the generality of section 22, the Assembly may\nalso make laws:\n(a) declaring the powers of the Assembly and of its members and\ncommittees, but so that the powers so declared do not exceed\n\n\nPowers of Legislative Assembly  Part IV\n\nSection 25\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nthe powers for the time being of the House of\nRepresentatives or of its members or committees; and\n(b) providing for the manner in which powers so declared may\nbe exercised or upheld.\n(3) Until the Assembly makes a law with respect to its powers, the\nAssembly and its members and committees have the same powers\nas the powers for the time being of the House of Representatives\nand its members and committees.\n(4) Nothing in this section empowers the Assembly to imprison or fine\na person."
    },
