    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Notification of enactment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a proposed law has been passed by the Assembly, the Chief\nMinister, or another person authorised by enactment to do so, shall\npublish in the Territory Gazette a notice of the proposed law\nhaving been passed and of the place or places where copies of the\nlaw can be purchased.\n(2) Where a proposed law is notified in the Territory Gazette, it takes\neffect upon the day of notification or, if the proposed law otherwise\nprovides, as so provided.\n(3) At the time of publication of the notice under subsection (1) of the\npassing of a proposed law or as soon as practicable thereafter,\ncopies of the law shall be made available for purchase at the place,\nor at each of the places, specified in the notice.\n(4) Where, on the day of publication of the notice under subsection (1)\nof the passing of a proposed law, there are no copies of the law\navailable for purchase at the place, or at one or more of the places,\nspecified in the notice, the Chief Minister shall cause to be laid\nbefore the Assembly, within 15 sitting days of the Assembly after\nthat day, a statement that copies of the law were not so available\nand the reason why they were not so available.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a proposed law has been passed by the Assembly, the Chief\nMinister, or another person authorised by enactment to do so, shall\npublish in the Territory Gazette a notice of the proposed law\nhaving been passed and of the place or places where copies of the\nlaw can be purchased.\n(2) Where a proposed law is notified in the Territory Gazette, it takes\neffect upon the day of notification or, if the proposed law otherwise\nprovides, as so provided.\n(3) At the time of publication of the notice under subsection (1) of the\npassing of a proposed law or as soon as practicable thereafter,\ncopies of the law shall be made available for purchase at the place,\nor at each of the places, specified in the notice.\n(4) Where, on the day of publication of the notice under subsection (1)\nof the passing of a proposed law, there are no copies of the law\navailable for purchase at the place, or at one or more of the places,\nspecified in the notice, the Chief Minister shall cause to be laid\nbefore the Assembly, within 15 sitting days of the Assembly after\nthat day, a statement that copies of the law were not so available\nand the reason why they were not so available.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-25-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-25-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-25-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-25-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aef451d326fbec48b3951e46b4ccaeac262f00502c12196196868219e6cd0cc4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Notification of enactment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a proposed law has been passed by the Assembly, the Chief\nMinister, or another person authorised by enactment to do so, shall\npublish in the Territory Gazette a notice of the proposed law\nhaving been passed and of the place or places where copies of the\nlaw can be purchased.\n(2) Where a proposed law is notified in the Territory Gazette, it takes\neffect upon the day of notification or, if the proposed law otherwise\nprovides, as so provided.\n(3) At the time of publication of the notice under subsection (1) of the\npassing of a proposed law or as soon as practicable thereafter,\ncopies of the law shall be made available for purchase at the place,\nor at each of the places, specified in the notice.\n(4) Where, on the day of publication of the notice under subsection (1)\nof the passing of a proposed law, there are no copies of the law\navailable for purchase at the place, or at one or more of the places,\nspecified in the notice, the Chief Minister shall cause to be laid\nbefore the Assembly, within 15 sitting days of the Assembly after\nthat day, a statement that copies of the law were not so available\nand the reason why they were not so available."
    },
