    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26(5) Special procedures for making certain enactments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-26-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If an entrenching law includes the requirement (however\nexpressed) that an enactment or enactments be passed by a\nspecified majority of the members (in this subsection called a\nspecial majority), the same requirement shall be taken to apply to\nthe entrenching law, so that it must be passed by:\n(a) that special majority; or\n(b) if it specifies different special majorities for different\nenactments—the highest of those special majorities.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If an entrenching law includes the requirement (however\nexpressed) that an enactment or enactments be passed by a\nspecified majority of the members (in this subsection called a\nspecial majority), the same requirement shall be taken to apply to\nthe entrenching law, so that it must be passed by:\n(a) that special majority; or\n(b) if it specifies different special majorities for different\nenactments—the highest of those special majorities.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c4948e421586b7f77cae6f0d1017ec7e5893d14640147496e5188a1b329818a8",
      "skos:note": "Entrenching law must be passed by a specified majority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-26-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26(5) Special procedures for making certain enactments",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If an entrenching law includes the requirement (however\nexpressed) that an enactment or enactments be passed by a\nspecified majority of the members (in this subsection called a\nspecial majority), the same requirement shall be taken to apply to\nthe entrenching law, so that it must be passed by:\n(a) that special majority; or\n(b) if it specifies different special majorities for different\nenactments—the highest of those special majorities."
    },
