      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) If an entrenching law includes the requirement..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26(6) Special procedures for making certain enactments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-26-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If an entrenching law passed by the Assembly:\n\n\nPowers of Legislative Assembly  Part IV\n\nSection 27\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(a) includes the requirement (however expressed) that an\nenactment or enactments be submitted to a referendum of the\nelectors of the Territory; and\n(b) includes provision (however expressed) that, to have effect,\nthe referendum is to be passed by a specified majority of the\nelectors (in this subsection called a special majority);\nthe same requirement shall be taken to apply to the entrenching\nlaw, so that the reference in subsection (3) to a majority of the\nelectors shall be taken to be a reference to:\n(c) that special majority; or\n(d) if the entrenching law specifies different special majorities\nfor different enactments—the highest of those special\nmajorities.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If an entrenching law passed by the Assembly:\n\n\nPowers of Legislative Assembly  Part IV\n\nSection 27\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(a) includes the requirement (however expressed) that an\nenactment or enactments be submitted to a referendum of the\nelectors of the Territory; and\n(b) includes provision (however expressed) that, to have effect,\nthe referendum is to be passed by a specified majority of the\nelectors (in this subsection called a special majority);\nthe same requirement shall be taken to apply to the entrenching\nlaw, so that the reference in subsection (3) to a majority of the\nelectors shall be taken to be a reference to:\n(c) that special majority; or\n(d) if the entrenching law specifies different special majorities\nfor different enactments—the highest of those special\nmajorities.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "52b8246323d35a95c9f52d1318c267d08bbe0d8c40c6f202169c29d60d2e0834",
      "skos:note": "Requirement for referendums on enactments under entrenching laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-26-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26(6) Special procedures for making certain enactments",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If an entrenching law passed by the Assembly:\n\n\nPowers of Legislative Assembly  Part IV\n\nSection 27\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(a) includes the requirement (however expressed) that an\nenactment or enactments be submitted to a referendum of the\nelectors of the Territory; and\n(b) includes provision (however expressed) that, to have effect,\nthe referendum is to be passed by a specified majority of the\nelectors (in this subsection called a special majority);\nthe same requirement shall be taken to apply to the entrenching\nlaw, so that the reference in subsection (3) to a majority of the\nelectors shall be taken to be a reference to:\n(c) that special majority; or\n(d) if the entrenching law specifies different special majorities\nfor different enactments—the highest of those special\nmajorities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-26-ss-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
