    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Inconsistency with other laws",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A provision of an enactment has no effect to the extent that it is\ninconsistent with a law defined by subsection (2), but such a\nprovision shall be taken to be consistent with such a law to the\nextent that it is capable of operating concurrently with that law.\n(2) In this section:\nlaw means:\n(a) a law in force in the Territory (other than an enactment or a\nsubordinate law); or\n(b) an order or determination, or any other instrument of a\nlegislative character, made under a law falling within\nparagraph (a).\nNote:\nSections 29 and 40 of the Fair Work Act 2009 deals with\ninconsistency between awards and agreements made under that Act,\nand laws of the Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A provision of an enactment has no effect to the extent that it is\ninconsistent with a law defined by subsection (2), but such a\nprovision shall be taken to be consistent with such a law to the\nextent that it is capable of operating concurrently with that law.\n(2) In this section:\nlaw means:\n(a) a law in force in the Territory (other than an enactment or a\nsubordinate law); or\n(b) an order or determination, or any other instrument of a\nlegislative character, made under a law falling within\nparagraph (a).\nNote:\nSections 29 and 40 of the Fair Work Act 2009 deals with\ninconsistency between awards and agreements made under that Act,\nand laws of the Territory.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-28-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-28-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4d8c64ccf23c22a954c7229633832bbd61736596abf7802f81b0ac2eec74c52e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Inconsistency with other laws",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A provision of an enactment has no effect to the extent that it is\ninconsistent with a law defined by subsection (2), but such a\nprovision shall be taken to be consistent with such a law to the\nextent that it is capable of operating concurrently with that law.\n(2) In this section:\nlaw means:\n(a) a law in force in the Territory (other than an enactment or a\nsubordinate law); or\n(b) an order or determination, or any other instrument of a\nlegislative character, made under a law falling within\nparagraph (a).\nNote:\nSections 29 and 40 of the Fair Work Act 2009 deals with\ninconsistency between awards and agreements made under that Act,\nand laws of the Territory."
    },
