    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Avoidance of application of enactments to Parliament",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\nenactment includes a part of an enactment.\nParliamentary precincts means the precincts defined by\nsubsection 3(1) of the Parliamentary Precincts Act 1988.\n(2) If either House of the Parliament passes a resolution declaring that\nan enactment made after the commencing day does not apply:\n(a) to that House;\n(b) to the members of that House; or\n(c) in the Parliamentary precincts;\nthe resolution has effect according to its tenor and the enactment\ndoes not apply accordingly.\n(3) A resolution under subsection (2):\n(a) does not have effect in respect of the application of an\nenactment on a day before the day on which the resolution is\npassed; and\n(b) has effect, to the extent that the enactment ceases to apply, as\nif the enactment were repealed by another enactment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this section:\nenactment includes a part of an enactment.\nParliamentary precincts means the precincts defined by\nsubsection 3(1) of the Parliamentary Precincts Act 1988.\n(2) If either House of the Parliament passes a resolution declaring that\nan enactment made after the commencing day does not apply:\n(a) to that House;\n(b) to the members of that House; or\n(c) in the Parliamentary precincts;\nthe resolution has effect according to its tenor and the enactment\ndoes not apply accordingly.\n(3) A resolution under subsection (2):\n(a) does not have effect in respect of the application of an\nenactment on a day before the day on which the resolution is\npassed; and\n(b) has effect, to the extent that the enactment ceases to apply, as\nif the enactment were repealed by another enactment.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-29-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "afdc2bb12b346b2674caf97b5d26cae6a36d51da078e697e2529095ac71ddfbe"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Avoidance of application of enactments to Parliament",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\nenactment includes a part of an enactment.\nParliamentary precincts means the precincts defined by\nsubsection 3(1) of the Parliamentary Precincts Act 1988.\n(2) If either House of the Parliament passes a resolution declaring that\nan enactment made after the commencing day does not apply:\n(a) to that House;\n(b) to the members of that House; or\n(c) in the Parliamentary precincts;\nthe resolution has effect according to its tenor and the enactment\ndoes not apply accordingly.\n(3) A resolution under subsection (2):\n(a) does not have effect in respect of the application of an\nenactment on a day before the day on which the resolution is\npassed; and\n(b) has effect, to the extent that the enactment ceases to apply, as\nif the enactment were repealed by another enactment."
    },
