    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-40",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40 Chief Minister for the Territory",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-40"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(1) At the first meeting of the Assembly after a general election, the\nmembers present shall, after electing a Presiding Officer and before\nany other business, elect one of their number to be the Chief\nMinister for the Territory.\n(2) If there is a vacancy in the office of Chief Minister (not because of\na dissolution of the Assembly), then:\n(a) if the vacancy happens at a meeting, the members present\nshall elect one of their number to be the Chief Minister; or\n(b) if the vacancy happens at any other time, the Presiding\nOfficer shall, by notice published in the Territory Gazette,\nconvene a meeting as soon as practicable and, at the meeting,\nthe members present shall elect one of their number to be the\nChief Minister.\n(3) If a resolution of no confidence in the Chief Minister is passed, the\nmembers present shall elect one of their number to be the Chief\nMinister.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) At the first meeting of the Assembly after a general election, the\nmembers present shall, after electing a Presiding Officer and before\nany other business, elect one of their number to be the Chief\nMinister for the Territory.\n(2) If there is a vacancy in the office of Chief Minister (not because of\na dissolution of the Assembly), then:\n(a) if the vacancy happens at a meeting, the members present\nshall elect one of their number to be the Chief Minister; or\n(b) if the vacancy happens at any other time, the Presiding\nOfficer shall, by notice published in the Territory Gazette,\nconvene a meeting as soon as practicable and, at the meeting,\nthe members present shall elect one of their number to be the\nChief Minister.\n(3) If a resolution of no confidence in the Chief Minister is passed, the\nmembers present shall elect one of their number to be the Chief\nMinister.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-40-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-40-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-40-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffab7b10a8cbe3b9bca6eae206fac0f5fdd607164e5754ad792ab62e86daf60b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-40",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40 Chief Minister for the Territory",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At the first meeting of the Assembly after a general election, the\nmembers present shall, after electing a Presiding Officer and before\nany other business, elect one of their number to be the Chief\nMinister for the Territory.\n(2) If there is a vacancy in the office of Chief Minister (not because of\na dissolution of the Assembly), then:\n(a) if the vacancy happens at a meeting, the members present\nshall elect one of their number to be the Chief Minister; or\n(b) if the vacancy happens at any other time, the Presiding\nOfficer shall, by notice published in the Territory Gazette,\nconvene a meeting as soon as practicable and, at the meeting,\nthe members present shall elect one of their number to be the\nChief Minister.\n(3) If a resolution of no confidence in the Chief Minister is passed, the\nmembers present shall elect one of their number to be the Chief\nMinister."
    },
