          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-40-ss-2-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2c68a6a8f3b0cf45e0ac674e26659eb49753fd56f7bc32775425650894dc9cda",
      "skos:note": "If there is a vacancy in the office of Chief Minister, the members present shall elect one of their number to be the Chief Minister."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-40-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40(2) Chief Minister for the Territory",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If there is a vacancy in the office of Chief Minister (not because of\na dissolution of the Assembly), then:\n(a) if the vacancy happens at a meeting, the members present\nshall elect one of their number to be the Chief Minister; or\n(b) if the vacancy happens at any other time, the Presiding\nOfficer shall, by notice published in the Territory Gazette,\nconvene a meeting as soon as practicable and, at the meeting,\nthe members present shall elect one of their number to be the\nChief Minister."
    },
