    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Vacation of office by Ministers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person holding office as Chief Minister vacates the office:\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n(c) immediately before a Chief Minister is elected after:\n(i) the next general election; or\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.\n(1A) A person holding office as a Minister (other than the Chief\nMinister) vacates the office:\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n(c) when the person is dismissed from office by the Chief\nMinister; or\n(d) immediately before another Chief Minister is elected after:\n(i) the next general election; or\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.\n(2) A person who has vacated an office of Minister may be re-elected\nor re-appointed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person holding office as Chief Minister vacates the office:\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n(c) immediately before a Chief Minister is elected after:\n(i) the next general election; or\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.\n(1A) A person holding office as a Minister (other than the Chief\nMinister) vacates the office:\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n(c) when the person is dismissed from office by the Chief\nMinister; or\n(d) immediately before another Chief Minister is elected after:\n(i) the next general election; or\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.\n(2) A person who has vacated an office of Minister may be re-elected\nor re-appointed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-46-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-46-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-46-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04e37efe1906a24f71b3b293b4f4b9b34a865b47b87434a7596e27d7acef7b73"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Vacation of office by Ministers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person holding office as Chief Minister vacates the office:\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n(c) immediately before a Chief Minister is elected after:\n(i) the next general election; or\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.\n(1A) A person holding office as a Minister (other than the Chief\nMinister) vacates the office:\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n(c) when the person is dismissed from office by the Chief\nMinister; or\n(d) immediately before another Chief Minister is elected after:\n(i) the next general election; or\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.\n(2) A person who has vacated an office of Minister may be re-elected\nor re-appointed."
    },
