    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48 Resolution of no confidence in Chief Minister",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n(a) on a particular day, the Assembly passes a resolution of no\nconfidence in the Chief Minister;\n(b) the Assembly does not, within the period of 30 days after that\nday, elect a Chief Minister; and\n(c) the Governor-General does not, within that period of 30 days,\ndissolve the Assembly under section 16;\na general election shall be held on a day specified by the\nCommonwealth Minister by notice published in the\nCommonwealth Gazette, being not earlier than 36 days, nor later\nthan 90 days, after the end of that period of 30 days.\n(3) The Commonwealth Minister shall not specify a day that is the\npolling day for an election of the Senate or a general election of the\nHouse of Representatives.\n\n\nThe Judiciary  Part VA\n\nSection 48A\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n(a) on a particular day, the Assembly passes a resolution of no\nconfidence in the Chief Minister;\n(b) the Assembly does not, within the period of 30 days after that\nday, elect a Chief Minister; and\n(c) the Governor-General does not, within that period of 30 days,\ndissolve the Assembly under section 16;\na general election shall be held on a day specified by the\nCommonwealth Minister by notice published in the\nCommonwealth Gazette, being not earlier than 36 days, nor later\nthan 90 days, after the end of that period of 30 days.\n(3) The Commonwealth Minister shall not specify a day that is the\npolling day for an election of the Senate or a general election of the\nHouse of Representatives.\n\n\nThe Judiciary  Part VA\n\nSection 48A\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bfeb5e85621f66de32c408be091eb9e5633c2e3a5614829277430e9285b28863"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48 Resolution of no confidence in Chief Minister",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n(a) on a particular day, the Assembly passes a resolution of no\nconfidence in the Chief Minister;\n(b) the Assembly does not, within the period of 30 days after that\nday, elect a Chief Minister; and\n(c) the Governor-General does not, within that period of 30 days,\ndissolve the Assembly under section 16;\na general election shall be held on a day specified by the\nCommonwealth Minister by notice published in the\nCommonwealth Gazette, being not earlier than 36 days, nor later\nthan 90 days, after the end of that period of 30 days.\n(3) The Commonwealth Minister shall not specify a day that is the\npolling day for an election of the Senate or a general election of the\nHouse of Representatives.\n\n\nThe Judiciary  Part VA\n\nSection 48A\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48-ss-2",
