    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48D Removal of a judicial officer from office",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-48d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "An enactment relating to the removal from office of a judicial\nofficer must provide that:\n(a) a judicial officer may only be removed from office if:\n(i) a judicial commission appointed by the Executive to\nexamine a complaint concerning the judicial officer has\nsubmitted to the Attorney-General of the Territory a\nreport that:\n(A) sets out the facts found by the commission in\nrelation to the subject matter of the complaint;\nand\n(B) states that, in the commission’s opinion, the\nfacts so found could amount to misbehaviour or\nphysical or mental incapacity (as the case may\n\n\nThe Judiciary  Part VA\n\nSection 48D\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nbe) warranting the officer’s removal from\noffice; and\n(ii) the Assembly:\n(A) has determined that the facts so found amount\nto misbehaviour or physical or mental\nincapacity identified by the commission; and\n(B) has passed a motion requiring the Executive to\nremove the officer from office on the ground of\nthat misbehaviour or incapacity; and\n(b) a judicial officer may only be removed from office by the\nExecutive in writing.",
      "skos:definition": "An enactment relating to the removal from office of a judicial\nofficer must provide that:\n(a) a judicial officer may only be removed from office if:\n(i) a judicial commission appointed by the Executive to\nexamine a complaint concerning the judicial officer has\nsubmitted to the Attorney-General of the Territory a\nreport that:\n(A) sets out the facts found by the commission in\nrelation to the subject matter of the complaint;\nand\n(B) states that, in the commission’s opinion, the\nfacts so found could amount to misbehaviour or\nphysical or mental incapacity (as the case may\n\n\nThe Judiciary  Part VA\n\nSection 48D\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nbe) warranting the officer’s removal from\noffice; and\n(ii) the Assembly:\n(A) has determined that the facts so found amount\nto misbehaviour or physical or mental\nincapacity identified by the commission; and\n(B) has passed a motion requiring the Executive to\nremove the officer from office on the ground of\nthat misbehaviour or incapacity; and\n(b) a judicial officer may only be removed from office by the\nExecutive in writing.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48d-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48d-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d1b81d9e1f547ad649b85152efc1e30a11b5687424e258217e87374ac88fb7de",
      "skos:note": "Judicial officer removal conditions",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-48d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48D Removal of a judicial officer from office",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "An enactment relating to the removal from office of a judicial\nofficer must provide that:\n(a) a judicial officer may only be removed from office if:\n(i) a judicial commission appointed by the Executive to\nexamine a complaint concerning the judicial officer has\nsubmitted to the Attorney-General of the Territory a\nreport that:\n(A) sets out the facts found by the commission in\nrelation to the subject matter of the complaint;\nand\n(B) states that, in the commission’s opinion, the\nfacts so found could amount to misbehaviour or\nphysical or mental incapacity (as the case may\n\n\nThe Judiciary  Part VA\n\nSection 48D\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nbe) warranting the officer’s removal from\noffice; and\n(ii) the Assembly:\n(A) has determined that the facts so found amount\nto misbehaviour or physical or mental\nincapacity identified by the commission; and\n(B) has passed a motion requiring the Executive to\nremove the officer from office on the ground of\nthat misbehaviour or incapacity; and\n(b) a judicial officer may only be removed from office by the\nExecutive in writing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-48d-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
