    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-65",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "65 Proposal of money votes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-65"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An enactment, vote or resolution (proposal) for the appropriation\nof the public money of the Territory must not be proposed in the\nAssembly except by a Minister.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent a member other than a Minister\nfrom moving an amendment to a proposal made by a Minister\nunless the amendment is to increase the amount of public money of\nthe Territory to be appropriated.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An enactment, vote or resolution (proposal) for the appropriation\nof the public money of the Territory must not be proposed in the\nAssembly except by a Minister.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent a member other than a Minister\nfrom moving an amendment to a proposal made by a Minister\nunless the amendment is to increase the amount of public money of\nthe Territory to be appropriated.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-65-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-65-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f5347882bb90756bb509c249704003492253bc9b1259426ce702810e18b9222"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-65",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "65 Proposal of money votes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An enactment, vote or resolution (proposal) for the appropriation\nof the public money of the Territory must not be proposed in the\nAssembly except by a Minister.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not prevent a member other than a Minister\nfrom moving an amendment to a proposal made by a Minister\nunless the amendment is to increase the amount of public money of\nthe Territory to be appropriated."
    },
