    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "67A General elections",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-67a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The members to be elected at a general election are to be elected as\nprovided by sections 67, 67C and 67D and by an enactment that:\n(a) provides for general elections; and\n(b) complies with section 67B; and\n(c) was made after polling day for the second general election.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The members to be elected at a general election are to be elected as\nprovided by sections 67, 67C and 67D and by an enactment that:\n(a) provides for general elections; and\n(b) complies with section 67B; and\n(c) was made after polling day for the second general election.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "32f016072428c9369dc0c523233bff47a49735237b3a6ea75822942d5d30f4df",
      "skos:note": "Members must be elected as provided by sections 67, 67C and 67D."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-67a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "67A General elections",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The members to be elected at a general election are to be elected as\nprovided by sections 67, 67C and 67D and by an enactment that:\n(a) provides for general elections; and\n(b) complies with section 67B; and\n(c) was made after polling day for the second general election."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to elect members",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "67B Electoral enactment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-67b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "An electoral enactment is to provide, among other things:\n(a) for the times of general elections; and\n\n\nElections to Assembly  Part VIII\n\nSection 67C\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(b) for a Roll of the electors of the Territory for the purposes of\ngeneral elections; and\n(c) that every person who is entitled to be enrolled on that Roll\nand who is resident in the Territory is required to claim\nenrolment; and\n(d) if the electoral enactment provides for the distribution of the\nTerritory into electorates—that a redistribution of the\nTerritory into electorates is to commence not later than 6\nyears after the previous distribution or redistribution.",
      "skos:definition": "An electoral enactment is to provide, among other things:\n(a) for the times of general elections; and\n\n\nElections to Assembly  Part VIII\n\nSection 67C\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(b) for a Roll of the electors of the Territory for the purposes of\ngeneral elections; and\n(c) that every person who is entitled to be enrolled on that Roll\nand who is resident in the Territory is required to claim\nenrolment; and\n(d) if the electoral enactment provides for the distribution of the\nTerritory into electorates—that a redistribution of the\nTerritory into electorates is to commence not later than 6\nyears after the previous distribution or redistribution.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2be2fbb55fc9f1c9332350b35a1b10b18e26b82e16ef055866bdf14ca7d6f126",
      "skos:note": "Every person who is entitled to be enrolled on the Roll of electors must claim enrolment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988#sch-5-sec-67b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "67B Electoral enactment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "An electoral enactment is to provide, among other things:\n(a) for the times of general elections; and\n\n\nElections to Assembly  Part VIII\n\nSection 67C\nAustralian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(b) for a Roll of the electors of the Territory for the purposes of\ngeneral elections; and\n(c) that every person who is entitled to be enrolled on that Roll\nand who is resident in the Territory is required to claim\nenrolment; and\n(d) if the electoral enactment provides for the distribution of the\nTerritory into electorates—that a redistribution of the\nTerritory into electorates is to commence not later than 6\nyears after the previous distribution or redistribution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-67b-norm",
